--- body ---
## Context
The specification chain makes claims about what Zotero and #6012 do. Two of
them were refuted at source on 2026-08-29 and a sweep of the rest found the
error rate is not incidental.

Sampled, with verdicts:

| site | claim | verdict |
|---|---|---|
| DESIGN.md:216 | "Zotero's geometry, adopted verbatim" | refuted (0140) |
| DESIGN.md:468 | "#6012's shipped geometry" (CJK 2-gram) | refuted (0060) |
| CONSTRAINTS.md C2 | geometry, and "never crosses a section" | refuted, fixed |
| DESIGN.md:417 | entry score is MAX over chunks, "#6012's rule" | holds |
| DESIGN.md:206 | prefix charged to the budget, "Zotero's own prior art" | holds in part |
| CONSTRAINTS.md:87 | rowid-constrained MATCH cost, "#6012's measurement" | mechanism holds, citation overstated — corrected |
| DESIGN.md:389 | "Zotero's own embeddings layer documents the same residue" | not supported at `77e2c4b` — removed |

The last two were settled at source on 2026-08-30 (see the log) and both are
now corrected in the text; the second row's coordinate had drifted from :321
to :389 since this table was written, which is its own argument for ticket
0181's guard.

**Five wrong out of eight**, counting only this ticket's class: the two
geometry refutations, C2's two claims, and the residue sentence, which said
Zotero's embeddings layer documents a staleness case it never addresses.
That is a class, not a run of bad luck, and the class has a shape worth
naming: **a value or behaviour is read from an upstream summary, adopted as
a constant, and cited as though the mechanism around it came too.** The
geometry case is the clearest — 768 was copied as a chunk size when upstream
uses it as a ceiling inside a `min()`, so the number arrived and the guard
that made it safe did not.

**The rowid row is a different defect and is deliberately not in that
count** (author's ruling, 2026-08-31). Its claim is TRUE — upstream states
it in as many words — and no implementer is misled by it. What was wrong was
the evidence grade: a rationale in a source comment was cited as a
measurement, so a reader credits the maintainer with numbers he never
published and assigns our claim more support than it has. Real, and worth
its own guard in ticket 0181, but folding it into the tally would blunt a
finding whose force comes from being about mechanism.

Why this is above the severity floor rather than a tidiness item. It bit the
science twice in one day: DESIGN.md §2.2 would have shipped a chunker that
silently truncates 60,6% of the corpus's text mass, and C2 told an
implementer the platform never crosses a section when it merges short ones
forward. It is also public text the upstream maintainer reads, and
misattributing his work is a cost this repo cannot pay twice.

## Actions
1. Enumerate every claim in REQUIREMENTS.md, CONSTRAINTS.md and DESIGN.md
   that asserts something about Zotero, #6012, or zoteus. The grep that
   found the sample above is a start, not the method: it keys on
   "verbatim / adopted / own / prior art / aligns with / #6012's" and will
   miss a claim phrased without those words.
2. For each, record the verdict and the coordinate that settles it — file,
   line, and the SHA read. A claim verified against PR head `77e2c4b` on
   2026-08-29 is verified *at that commit*, and #6012 is an open draft that
   moves.
3. Correct what is wrong. Anything that changes a ratified reading goes to
   DECISIONS.md first.
4. For the two unverified entries above, either verify or mark them as
   unverified in the text. "Could not look" stated is better than a claim
   the reader takes as established.

## Test
This is an audit, not code. Its check is that every surviving attribution
carries a coordinate, which ticket 0181 turns into a standing guard.

## Verification
- [ ] Every external attribution has a verdict and a coordinate
- [ ] Unverified claims say so in the text
- [ ] Corrections that touch ratified readings went through DECISIONS.md

## Invariants
- Read source, not a summary. A WebFetch of a PR page is weaker evidence
  than the file at a SHA, and the difference is what produced this ticket.
- A null is not a refutation: a claim a grep cannot find may still be true
  elsewhere in the tree. Mark unverified, not false.
- Nothing here is filed upstream; the PR budget is untouched.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The enumeration is complete and recorded
- [ ] Every claim is verified, corrected, or marked unverified
- [ ] `make check` passes
